racking-wide heading-font mb-1">Risk Management</h5><p class="text-white/40 text-xs leading-relaxed">Reduce clinical risks and improve patient outcomes through systematic quality management.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-2 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 flex flex-col justify-center"><h3 class="heading-font text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">Choosing an assessment route</h3><p class="text-white/45 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">Confirm the applicable criteria, proposed healthcare scope and audit arrangements before beginning an assessment.</p><p class="text-white/45 text-sm leading-relaxed">Certification availability and accreditation status depend on the selected scheme and scope. Verify current credentials before relying on a certification claim.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="text-center mb-8"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Explore More</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">Related Certifications</h2></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5 max-w-4xl mx-auto"><a class="group relative h-[280px] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 hover:border-euro-300 shadow-md hover:shadow-xl transition-all duration-500" href="/management-system/iso-9001/"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-110" style="background-image:url(&#x27;https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367536/eurocert/m2.png.png&#x27;)"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[#030a16]/80 via-[#030a16]/20 to-transparent"></div><div class="absolute bottom-5 left-5 right-5 z-20"><h4 class="text-white text-sm heading-font font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">ISO 9001</h4><span class="text-[9px] font-bold uppercase text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.2em] heading-font">Quality Management</span></div></a><a class="group relative h-[280px] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 hover:border-euro-300 shadow-md hover:shadow-xl transition-all duration-500" href="/management-system/iso-14001/"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-110" style="background-image:url(&#x27;https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367542/eurocert/m3.png.png&#x27;)"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[#030a16]/80 via-[#030a16]/20 to-transparent"></div><div class="absolute bottom-5 left-5 right-5 z-20"><h4 class="text-white text-sm heading-font font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">ISO 14001</h4><span class="text-[9px] font-bold uppercase text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.2em] heading-font">Environmental Management</span></div></a><a class="group relative h-[280px] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 hover:border-euro-300 shadow-md hover:shadow-xl transition-all duration-500" href="/management-system/iso-45001/"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-110" style="background-image:url(&#x27;https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367547/eurocert/m4.png.png&#x27;)"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[#030a16]/80 via-[#030a16]/20 to-transparent"></div><div class="absolute bottom-5 left-5 right-5 z-20"><h4 class="text-white text-sm heading-font font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">ISO 45001</h4><span class="text-[9px] font-bold uppercase text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.2em] heading-font">OH&amp;S Management</span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#030a16]"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_bottom,rgba(212,168,67,0.06)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div><div class="relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-18"><div class="container mx-auto px-6 text-center"><div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto p-10 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-3 font-bold">Get Certified</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">Quick Inquiry</h2><p class="text-white/45 mb-6 max-w-lg mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Discuss the standard, healthcare scope and applicable audit criteria for your organisation.</p><div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#030a16] bg-eurogold-400 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-eurogold-300 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-eurogold-400/20" href="/contact/">Get Started <i class="fas fa-arrow-right text-[9px]"></i></a><a href="tel:+919316012883" onclick="return gtag_report_conversion('tel:+919316012883');" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white border border-white/15 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all"><i class="fas fa-phone text-[9px]"></i> Call Us Now</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white" aria-labelledby="standard-details"><div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl space-y-8"><h2 id="standard-details" class="heading-font text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Applying EN 15224:2016 and healthcare quality management in practice</h2><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Who should consider it?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Hospitals, clinics, diagnostic and imaging services, laboratories, rehabilitation providers, dental services, care organisations and other healthcare providers may use EN 15224 to structure quality across clinical and supporting processes. Multi-site organisations should define the legal entities, locations, services and outsourced activities included. Suppliers can clarify quality responsibilities where their work affects care, but their inclusion should be justified by the scope.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Key requirements</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed"><li>Understand organizational context and interested parties; set healthcare-relevant policy, responsibilities and measurable quality objectives.</li><li>Map care pathways and supporting processes, control handovers, referrals, continuity and outsourced services.</li><li>Identify clinical risks and opportunities, including risks to patient safety, care availability and continuity, and apply proportionate controls.</li><li>Monitor patient and service-user feedback, complaints, incidents and process performance; investigate causes and use findings to improve.</li><li>Maintain competence, resources, documented information, internal audit and management review, integrating the system with routine clinical governance.</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Certification and audit lifecycle</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Confirm that the proposed scope and requested assessment route are covered by an appropriate scheme and competent certification body. For a formal management-system certification audit, stage 1 reviews scope, system design, documented information and readiness, identifying issues for resolution before the main audit. Stage 2 evaluates implementation and effectiveness by sampling processes, staff understanding, records, relevant services and sites. Nonconformities must be addressed under the scheme before an independent certification decision. Surveillance audits then check continued conformity at planned intervals, and recertification is considered before the cycle ends where the scheme provides it. An audit is not a clinical-outcome guarantee. Timing depends on sites, service range, workforce, outsourcing, clinical risk and scheme rules; no fixed duration should be assumed.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Documents to prepare</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Prepare the scope and site list; context and interested-party analysis; process and care-pathway maps; quality policy and objectives; clinical-risk assessments; obligations register; roles and competence records; supplier controls; monitoring and patient-feedback data; complaints and incident records; internal-audit programme and reports; management-review minutes; and corrective actions. Protect patient information and agree secure, necessary sampling.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Frequently asked questions</h3><div class="space-y-4"><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Is EN 15224 only for hospitals?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. It may apply to different healthcare organisations and service types; suitability depends on services, boundaries, risks and locations in scope.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Does it replace ISO 9001?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">It builds on the ISO 9001 quality-management framework and adds healthcare-specific requirements; it does not replace clinical protocols, laws or professional standards.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Does certification prove every clinical outcome is good?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. An audit samples a management system against defined criteria and cannot guarantee individual outcomes or replace clinical evaluation and regulatory oversight.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">How long does certification take?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">There is no universal duration. Preparation and audit time depend on scope, locations, service complexity, system maturity and scheme rules.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">What follows the initial audit?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Where certification is granted, surveillance checks ongoing conformity at planned intervals and recertification is considered before the cycle ends, subject to the scheme.</p></article></div></div></div></section>
